\DOC DISCARD_ASSUMPTIONS_TAC

\TYPE {DISCARD_ASSUMPTIONS_TAC : (thm -> bool) -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Deletes from the goal's assumption list every assumption whose theorem
satisfies the supplied predicate, leaving the conclusion unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {P : thm -> bool} is applied to each assumption viewed as a
theorem; every assumption for which it holds is removed. In the observed traces
the predicates test the conclusion's free variables, its shape, or match it
against a list of patterns.
{
          A ?- t
     ===============  DISCARD_ASSUMPTIONS_TAC P
          A' ?- t
}
\noindent Here {A'} is {A} minus the assumptions satisfying {P}, with the
survivors in their original relative order. The removed set may be empty, in
which case the goal is returned unchanged; it may equally range from a single
assumption up to most of a large assumption list. Nothing is ever added, and
the conclusion is never touched.

\COMMENTS
Across all observed traces, the only behaviour shown is this in-place filtering
of assumptions yielding one subgoal.

\ENDDOC
